   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Finished past and experience",
     "texto": [
      "The past tense usually goes with a finished, specific moment: **Jeg besøkte Bergen i fjor** («I visited Bergen last year»). The perfect (**har + participle**) can highlight a relevant experience now or an action whose period continues: **Jeg har besøkt Bergen flere ganger** («I've visited Bergen several times»).",
      "Expressions help, but they don't mechanically determine the form: **i fjor** usually marks a closed period; **ennå ikke** is common with the perfect. Choose according to the time frame you want to give."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
